 "findings": [
  "A model-inference endpoint is reachable from exactly one file inside those entry closures: astra_runtime.py itself (https://text.pollinations.ai/ used as fallback, and as the labelled planner_source). Its path is gated by allow_optional_model_planner and by ASTRA_DISABLE_MODEL_PLANNER, and it labels its own output MODEL_ASSISTED.",
  "The V19 OSWorld subject and the V3 submission entrypoint reach no inference endpoint: 50 and 24 modules, zero endpoint files. The same holds for the research source frontend, the environment broker, and the scan/retrieve/fetch tool.",
  "The selected OSWorld route (V19) is not what the committed submission entrypoints import: v1 imports subject v1 and v3 imports subject v3. No entrypoint imports v19. A benchmark claim naming V19 would not be the route the submitted entrypoint runs.",
  "osworld_v21_brain_subject_v19.py does not import in this sandbox: canonical/runtime/osworld_v21_visual_region_grounding_v1.py raises ModuleNotFoundError: No module named PIL. Static reachability is not importability.",
  "The vendored model clients (stirrup openrouter/slack, minisweagent openrouter/requesty) are unreachable from every audited entry; they are evaluator-side trees, not runtime."
 ],
